 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Unweighted Trilinear Interpolation Volume Rendering
-A volume rendering method where voxel material colors are obtained via color transfer function without opacity weighting, lighting is calculated per voxel, and then colors are interpolated to resampling points [S2]. It produces 'intermediate colors' at interfaces between different media because transparent media influence voxel color too much when color is not opacity-weighted [S2]. It calculates lighting for each of the 8 voxels before interpolation, resulting in 8 lighting model calculations per resampling point, whereas the opacity-weighted method calculates lighting only once [S2].
